<!DOCTYPE html>
<%# The error page for when the normal page shell cannot be trusted: the
    failure happened before the page settings (language, theme, user) were
    loaded, which is exactly what happens when the database is down, because
    the session is read from it first. Sept 29: the database hit its free-tier
    quota, the normal error page then crashed on a missing setting, and
    everybody got a bare "Internal Server Error" with no explanation. This
    page needs nothing but the two values passed to it. %>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8" />
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
  <title><%= title %> · Sampaguita HC</title>
  <link rel="icon" href="/favicon.png" type="image/png" />
  <style>
    body { margin: 0; min-height: 100vh; display: grid; place-items: center; padding: 24px;
           font-family: system-ui, -apple-system, "Segoe UI", sans-serif; background: #eef3ee; color: #1b2a1d; }
    .box { max-width: 440px; background: #fff; border: 1px solid #d9e4d9; border-radius: 16px; padding: 28px; text-align: center; }
    .box img { width: 64px; height: 64px; }
    h1 { font-size: 20px; margin: 12px 0 8px; }
    p { font-size: 14.5px; line-height: 1.55; color: #45574a; margin: 0 0 10px; }
    .tl { font-size: 13.5px; color: #6b7c6f; }
    a { display: inline-block; margin-top: 10px; background: #2e7d32; color: #fff; text-decoration: none;
        font-weight: 700; padding: 10px 18px; border-radius: 10px; }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <div class="box">
    <img src="/img/barangay-seal-160.png" alt="" />
    <h1><%= title %></h1>
    <p><%= message %></p>
    <% if (typeof messageTl !== "undefined" && messageTl) { %><p class="tl"><%= messageTl %></p><% } %>
    <a href="/">Try again</a>
  </div>
</body>
</html>
